ebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5395e878ba6761d5aafdfbd4ee6500f12904f78ae0d9b980c91748410fc3516c","event_uuid":"89bf9198-ed83-44af-a9a0-79591f970123","position":{"commit_sha":"144fa077dc6ca0493edb7afc371bbaa1dac391ef","position":"1785806597025814001-89bf9198-ed83-44af-a9a0-79591f970123"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"253f563bca7edcea38272cfd1a1316eca0102066be645e22d34731548176a3d7","event_uuid":"2d0cae5a-f5b2-45c1-b5c8-3bb505b12567","position":{"commit_sha":"dc8c58f6fe68a982b4a7d1ed8e7acc696daace5f","position":"1785807798277990001-2d0cae5a-f5b2-45c1-b5c8-3bb505b12567"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Replaced the 24-hour proxy with direct writer evidence and a compatibility-preserving contract. The implementation must retain max(sidecar, legacy), promote any later legacy stamp into get_rotation.json, scrub the inline field, and prove an old/new writer sequence converges. Closure still requires descendant reconcile-workflow evidence plus explicit host probe refresh and no older process.","timestamp":1785780491351253001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation applied. The save contract is now sidecar-first: set_last_get stages an inline failure floor, save promotes chronological max to get_rotation.json, and only a successful sidecar persist permits inline scrub. A fail-open sidecar write retains the inline floor; a crash after sidecar replace is also safe because the max is already durable. Added explicit failure/crash integration oracles and scoped rollback support to A2-1-or-newer binaries; pre-A2-1 rollback loses only bounded rotation optimization and is prohibited after the deployment gate. Re-review required before claim.","timestamp":1785801293530619001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan review PASS, blocking=0. Advisory P6 accepted without plan mutation: the compound AC clauses deliberately describe one atomic precondition/failure/recovery state transition and one test must prove the whole invariant; splitting them into independently checkable boxes could certify only half the safety contract. The phrase “as needed” is confined to the non-binding Files note, not implementation behavior or an AC.","timestamp":1785801610506832001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A2-2 RED oracle established at base 5892134975. Contract cards: (1) normal cutover: mixed inline/sidecar store -> BindingStore.save -> sidecar holds chronological max, bindings retain all unrelated fields but no inline stamps, reload order exact; (2) fail-open recovery: inject get_rotation tempfile failure -> primary save retains newest inline floor, reload exact, clean retry converges sidecar-only; (3) crash boundary: inject bindings os.replace failure after sidecar boundary -> bindings bytes unchanged, newest max already durable in sidecar, reload/retry converges; (4) real-git commit boundary -> one commit contains scrubbed bindings plus max sidecar and clean worktree. Six selected new/strengthened nodes collected/executed with no skip/xfail and failed for intended behavior absence: 6 failed in 1.70s (five legacy-field assertions, one bindings-first crash-max assertion). Existing anti-starvation test remains the green regression guard; packed cost is a post-GREEN repository measurement. Surface census: CLI no direct surface (reconciler internal); MCP/API and public library out of scope (no binding-store surface); automated reconciler caller in scope via real commit boundary; dual-direction in scope through old-writer/new-writer max migration. Contention suite exempt: one established save boundary, no new lock/retry/cache layer.","timestamp":1785801780545683001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out validation GREEN on first standard-tier implementation attempt: six original hidden happy/edge/crash/E2E nodes passed in 0.73s; defect-seeded bindings-first mutation drove the crash-boundary node RED and restoration returned green. Five-axis review found one missing sidecar-os.replace recovery case; under revert-first discipline it failed against pre-fix ordering, passed after restoration, and the full focused regression set is now 20 passed in 1.02s. Refactoring litmus: assertions target persisted JSON, reload ordering, real git commit contents, and exact fault boundaries, not private source structure. Implementer tier: standard/mid gpt-5.6-terra, one attempt; it saw only the happy-path test. Packed-cost measurement is deterministic across two runs on the pinned 40-revision corpus 46a2426a..5282e235: A2-1 1728.74 bytes/changed version, A2-2 1286.05, ratio 0.7439; A2-2 is ~10.1% of the epic 12.79 KB baseline. Command and method are recorded in docs/experiments/bridge-state-get-rotation-cutover.md.","timestamp":1785802592627795001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Full preflight PASS on base 5892134975: make test completed with 9730 passed, 42 skipped, 192 deselected, 17 warnings in 1940.23s; exit 0. Earlier gates remain green: make lint, make typecheck, focused 20-test regression, module-size checks, script Ruff, git diff --check, deterministic packed-cost measurement. origin/main was fetched afterward and is three non-overlapping commits ahead; next step is isolated-worktree fast-forward plus post-update regression before commit.","timestamp":1785804608277592001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final exact-base preflight PASS after fast-forward to origin/main 1d136b8db5: make test completed with 9785 passed, 34 skipped, 192 deselected, 17 warnings in 1943.02s; exit 0. Post-update focused rotation oracle: 11 passed. make lint, make typecheck, module-size checks, script Ruff, git diff --check, and secret-pattern scan also pass. Five-axis review: no required correctness/readability/architecture/security/performance finding; persistence ordering retains the maximum at every observable file boundary, tests are behavior-facing, and no dependency was added.","timestamp":1785806597025814001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Rollout precheck on updated origin/main found the host updater still pinned at d72c4777 because its 2026-08-04 01:27 launchd install requested the now-explicitly-incompatible dev+eval extras; uv proved the boto3 constraint conflict. Created bug 4ba4-8086-8665-4303 and linked it discovered_from this ticket. A2-2 remains open until a real launchd refresh succeeds and provenance/process evidence is recorded.","timestamp":1785807798277990001}],"created_at":1785372494855599001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a8f84eaa-99f7-482a-aa58-b36b329839d2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5fa1-aab2-e6b5-4fad"},{"link_uuid":"be3b9dfc-8305-4396-b5e9-6dae225ac5bc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e6b7-e618-9d47-429a"}],"description":"Complete A2 by removing the steady-state legacy field, so successful new-writer passes leave `bindings.json` with no rotation bookkeeping. This is the irreversible half of A2. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** contains the measured facts; do not re-derive them.\n\n## Compatibility and evidence gate (no fixed delay)\n\n- A2-1 is merged to `main`.\n- A completed `reconcile-bridge.yml` run has a `github.sha` that is a descendant of the A2-1 merge commit (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). The workflow installs from that checked-out tree, so this directly proves the ephemeral writer executed the sidecar-capable build.\n- Before closure, explicitly refresh the host probe binary from a descendant of the A2-1 merge, record its executable path and version/source, and prove no older reconcile/probe process remains. Do not substitute elapsed time for these observations.\n\nThe writer set is the GHA reconciler and local probe runs. The canary runs only `bridge-fsck` plus ticket CLI operations; the AWS review bot never writes `bindings.json`. Mixed-version safety remains in code: a legacy writer may temporarily reintroduce an inline stamp, but the next new writer reads `max(sidecar, legacy)`, stages that maximum in both in-memory forms, persists the sidecar first, and scrubs the inline field only after sidecar persistence succeeds. An overlooked old process therefore causes bounded churn and self-heals instead of losing rotation progress.\n\nThe supported rollback floor after A2-2 is the A2-1 merge: any A2-1-or-newer binary reads both forms. A rollback below A2-1 is deliberately unsupported after the deployment evidence gate. Such a pre-sidecar binary would see scrubbed inline state as empty and forfeit only the rotation optimization, causing bounded extra GETs and rebuilding coverage within `ceil(N/K)` passes; it does not lose bindings or reconciliation correctness.\n\n## Persistence ordering and failure contract\n\nA successful save must establish this order:\n\n1. Merge every staged inline value into the in-memory sidecar using chronological `max`.\n2. Atomically persist `get_rotation.json`.\n3. Only when sidecar persistence returns `True`, remove inline `last_get_pass` values and atomically write `bindings.json`.\n\n`set_last_get` continues staging the inline value in memory as a failure floor; the successful save path removes it before `bindings.json` is serialized, so steady-state committed output remains sidecar-only. If the fail-open sidecar write returns `False`, the same save retains and writes the inline values to `bindings.json`. If the process fails after the sidecar replace but before the bindings replace, the sidecar already contains the maximum and the old bindings file still contains its legacy floor. Thus every observable one-file or two-file state retains the maximum, and the next successful new-writer pass converges to sidecar-only form.\n\n## Approach\n\nChange `BindingStore.save()` to persist rotation state before serializing the inline-scrubbed binding payload. Keep the mixed-version `max(new, legacy)` read seam. On sidecar failure, persist the binding payload with inline fallback values intact; on the next successful pass, promote their maximum and scrub them. Do not make ordinary reconciliation fail because rotation is an optimization, but do not discard the only durable copy of its maximum.\n\n## Verification plan\n\n- Normal success: a real temporary store advances rotation, saves, reloads with inline fields absent, and preserves exact rotation order from `get_rotation.json`.\n- Fail-open sidecar write: inject a sidecar tempfile/replace failure, prove the primary binding save succeeds with the latest inline floor retained, reload with identical order, then remove the fault and prove the next save promotes and scrubs it.\n- Mid-save crash boundary: let the sidecar replace succeed, inject failure at the subsequent bindings replace, and prove a fresh reload returns the same maximum and rotation order before a later successful convergence.\n- Mixed writer: a legacy writer reintroduces a later inline stamp; the new writer persists that maximum before scrubbing and matches an all-new sequence.\n- Anti-starvation and repository packed-size measurements remain the end-to-end behavior and cost oracles.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] After one successful new-writer save, `last_get_pass` is absent from every entry in `bindings.json`, the sidecar contains the chronological maximum, and rotation order is preserved after reload. Tier: integration in a real temporary git repository.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] When sidecar persistence fails open, the primary binding save succeeds with the latest inline fallback retained; reload preserves the same rotation order, and the next successful save promotes the maximum to `get_rotation.json` before removing the inline field. Tier: integration with injected tempfile and replace failures.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A failure after the sidecar replace but before the bindings replace cannot lose the maximum: a fresh reload observes the same maximum and a later successful save converges to sidecar-only form. Tier: integration at the two-file persistence boundary.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Anti-starvation still holds: every bound-but-absent key is serviced within `ceil(N/K)` passes with only the new file present. Tier: unit on the rotation selector.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An old-writer/new-writer sequence that reintroduces a later inline stamp migrates that maximum into `get_rotation.json`, removes the inline field, and preserves the same subsequent rotation order as an all-new sequence. Tier: integration.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Gate evidence is recorded on this ticket: A2-1 merge SHA, descendant `reconcile-bridge.yml` run id and successful ancestry result, host probe executable/version after an explicit refresh, and confirmation that no older reconcile/probe process remains.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Marginal packed cost per changed version is at or below the A2-1 measurement. Tier: repository-level measurement.\n\n## Files\n\n`binding_store.py`, existing rotation helpers as needed, and focused unit/integration tests.\n\nScope: S. Depends on A3 (sequencing A1 -> A2-1 -> A3 -> A2-2).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"stop writing the legacy field"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","5fa1-aab2-e6b5-4fad"],["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"],["relates_to","e6b7-e618-9d47-429a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"b2e0fb8d-73e2-4055-b3ba-82cac41eccbd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3592-0d1e-2bd6-4e22","ticket_type":"story","title":"A2-2: delete the legacy in-line last_get_pass field once every writer is upgraded","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["864e640f-dc02-4d81-a8e9-cde882e2203d","e754cca3-2d69-4a7a-b6c7-7fcbe15db163","be73fe7a-9908-4f38-96c8-a5881cc25a19","a8f84eaa-99f7-482a-aa58-b36b329839d2","c5e9b4b3-8b0b-4bb1-9193-2af9e6e61fc2","c93ecad5-cc50-4ca0-8ac0-d4d5ec567128","0b17472d-21b9-41da-bd1a-e5a7de7ff273","bdcbfab2-eee1-4302-a989-146fa5ffc95c","f9b4346e-3ef8-49af-b5c1-bfaada7f3c27","3f4ea335-8486-4bd9-acc2-ed156f975892","b2e0fb8d-73e2-4055-b3ba-82cac41eccbd","dfe522b4-191b-461e-a686-92f0949451cd","ccb154ee-d74a-4f0c-8604-9bb37afb9feb","ab4c45e5-3b56-4a3c-a966-ddfa26eb8eef","6c3ec6bf-1379-4444-a2ef-81cde9f1bb77","89bf9198-ed83-44af-a9a0-79591f970123","be3b9dfc-8305-4396-b5e9-6dae225ac5bc","2d0cae5a-f5b2